  "description": "FOHZAH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C70 H86 Br6 Cl2 Dy6 N6 O22 2+,2(C2 H6 O1),4(C2 H3 N1),2(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.492-3.867 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.76-112.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C82H110Dy6N10O24Cl4Br6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
